# Gates this repository subscribes to. One per line: <gate> [args]
# Catalog, contract, and how to run these locally: https://github.com/Greenbauer/vibe-verifier
# The job runs on GitHub's hosted runner on purpose: this repository is public, and a self-hosted
# runner on a public repository would run any fork's pull request on the operator's machine.
gitleaks
actionlint
zizmor
# cognitive-complexity and bandit ratchet per file: what main already has never blocks, a pull
# request that adds an over-limit function or a new finding does.
cognitive-complexity
bandit
osv-scanner
# prose: an em dash, or an en dash used as an aside, on a Markdown line a pull request adds blocks (house
# style); a curly quote and the pull request description are advisory. Only added lines count.
prose
# max-file-lines is NOT subscribed: mix.py is about 3,800 lines, so every change to it would block.
# Subscribe it once mix.py is split into modules.
